<http://data.silknow.org/object/fce061d4-0f7f-35c1-8719-245f543b0057/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning and running stitch with a facing of silk satin and a backing of silk satin.\nIn each of the four corners of the field is an 8-pointed light blue star showing a seated angel by a small pond containing a fish and flanked by curved floral stems.  Over the head is a heron-like bird. Between these stars are rectangles with triangular points projecting from each side, containing 2 fish and floral stems on either a light blue or a faded pink ground.  In the centre is a small circle also containing fish and floral ornaments.  The rest of the field is decorated with floral sprays on a black ground.  There is a narrow border with a repeating design of cypresses and animals [deer?].\nIn the corner with the Museum Number, the design continues but with a change in the field with a different shade of red which may be the product of a different type of dye.\nThe pattern in the border seems slightly truncated along the edges and it may have been cut.\nFacing: bias-cut faded blue satin.\nBacking: light blue satin.\nEmbroidery Thread: 2S silk; black, pink, red, light and dark blue, cream, light brown, shades of yellow."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/fce061d4-0f7f-35c1-8719-245f543b0057> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/d27f3328-ff0a-3cea-a224-265d18dd90e4>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "This embroidery belongs to Group 2 as defined by Jennifer Wearden in 'Azerbaijanian Embroideries: A Synthesis of Contrasts' in Hali Issue 59, October 1991 pp.102-111.  Group 2 textiles from the earlier 18th century are characterised by  surface darning with dark, strong colours."@en ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/fce061d4-0f7f-35c1-8719-245f543b0057> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/information/bibliography> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "This embroidery belongs to Group 2 as defined by Jennifer Wearden in 'Azerbaijanian Embroideries: A Synthesis of Contrasts' in Hali Issue 59, October 1991 pp.102-111.  Group 2 textiles from the earlier 18th century are characterised by  surface darning with dark, strong colours."@en .

