<http://data.silknow.org/object/fce061d4-0f7f-35c1-8719-245f543b0057>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning and running stitch with a facing of silk satin and a backing of silk satin.\nIn each of the four corners of the field is an 8-pointed light blue star showing a seated angel by a small pond containing a fish and flanked by curved floral stems.  Over the head is a heron-like bird. Between these stars are rectangles with triangular points projecting from each side, containing 2 fish and floral stems on either a light blue or a faded pink ground.  In the centre is a small circle also containing fish and floral ornaments.  The rest of the field is decorated with floral sprays on a black ground.  There is a narrow border with a repeating design of cypresses and animals [deer?].\nIn the corner with the Museum Number, the design continues but with a change in the field with a different shade of red which may be the product of a different type of dye.\nThe pattern in the border seems slightly truncated along the edges and it may have been cut.\nFacing: bias-cut faded blue satin.\nBacking: light blue satin.\nEmbroidery Thread: 2S silk; black, pink, red, light and dark blue, cream, light brown, shades of yellow."@en , "Middle East, Textile; Panel, silk-embroidered cotton, design of four star-medallions with seated angels, and four cartouches with paired fish, all set around a central roundel, on black ground with red border, Azerbaijan or NW Iran, 1700-1725"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/70527ea6-74b6-3bc5-8785-5d5a5deae392> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/30aa8838-d888-3ca5-97bc-2eb24124492d> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/786fcb4d-d50a-398e-b1ef-db0a53988b2a> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/572e262e-de9b-39b3-93a5-2dcaee8a1c14> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/c2647f33-69fc-3522-86db-37d522cfbdaf> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning and running stitch with a facing of silk satin and a backing of silk satin.\nIn each of the four corners of the field is an 8-pointed light blue star showing a seated angel by a small pond containing a fish and flanked by curved floral stems.  Over the head is a heron-like bird. Between these stars are rectangles with triangular points projecting from each side, containing 2 fish and floral stems on either a light blue or a faded pink ground.  In the centre is a small circle also containing fish and floral ornaments.  The rest of the field is decorated with floral sprays on a black ground.  There is a narrow border with a repeating design of cypresses and animals [deer?].\nIn the corner with the Museum Number, the design continues but with a change in the field with a different shade of red which may be the product of a different type of dye.\nThe pattern in the border seems slightly truncated along the edges and it may have been cut.\nFacing: bias-cut faded blue satin.\nBacking: light blue satin.\nEmbroidery Thread: 2S silk; black, pink, red, light and dark blue, cream, light brown, shades of yellow."@en , "Middle East, Textile; Panel, silk-embroidered cotton, design of four star-medallions with seated angels, and four cartouches with paired fish, all set around a central roundel, on black ground with red border, Azerbaijan or NW Iran, 1700-1725"@en ;
